@startuml sequence-autoprep-ia
!theme cerulean-outline
title FlipLearn — Séquence "Auto-préparation IA d'une capsule" (5 appels Groq parallèles)

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor<<prof>> #FEF3C7
  BorderColor<<prof>> #B45309
  BackgroundColor<<front>> #E0F2FE
  BorderColor<<front>> #0369A1
  BackgroundColor<<api>> #DCFCE7
  BorderColor<<api>> #166534
  BackgroundColor<<service>> #F3E8FF
  BorderColor<<service>> #7C3AED
  BackgroundColor<<ai>> #FAE8FF
  BorderColor<<ai>> #A21CAF
  BackgroundColor<<db>> #FEF3C7
  BorderColor<<db>> #B45309
}

actor "Professeur\n(omar)" as Prof <<prof>>
participant "AutoPrepReview.jsx\n(React)" as Front <<front>>
participant "courseAutoPrep\nController" as API <<api>>
participant "courseAutoPrep\nService" as Service <<service>>
participant "Whisper\n(OpenAI)" as Whisper <<ai>>
participant "Groq Llama-3.3" as Groq <<ai>>
database "MongoDB" as DB <<db>>

== Démarrage du job ==

Prof -> Front: clique "✨ IA" sur capsule
activate Front
Front -> API: POST /api/courses/:cid/videos/:vid/auto-prep
activate API
API -> API: vérifie quota (5/jour/prof)
API -> DB: AutoPrepJob.create\n{ status: 'pending' }
activate DB
DB --> API: jobId
deactivate DB
API --> Front: 202 { jobId }
Front -> Front: setJobId(...)\nstart polling

== Récupération transcript ==

API -> Service: runJob(jobId) [async]
activate Service
Service -> DB: VideoAnalysis.findOne(\n  { videoId })
activate DB
DB --> Service: existingAnalysis ?
deactivate DB

alt analyse Whisper inexistante
  Service -> Whisper: transcribe(videoUrl)
  activate Whisper
  Whisper --> Service: transcript text
  deactivate Whisper
  Service -> DB: VideoAnalysis.create
end

== 5 appels Groq parallèles ==

Service -> Service: const tasks = [\n  generateInVideoQuestions,\n  generateQCM,\n  generateOutcomes,\n  generatePrositIdea,\n  generateFlashcards\n]

note right of Service #FFFAE6
  **Promise.allSettled([5 tâches])**
  → robustesse : 1 échec parmi 5
  ne fait pas échouer le pipeline.
  Le prof récupère les 4 valides.
end note

par Appel parallèle 1 — InVideoQuestions
  Service -> Groq: prompt + transcript
  Groq --> Service: questions[] (timestamps)
also Appel 2 — QCM
  Service -> Groq: prompt + transcript
  Groq --> Service: qcm 10 questions
also Appel 3 — Outcomes Bloom
  Service -> Groq: prompt + transcript
  Groq --> Service: outcomes 3-5 niveaux
also Appel 4 — Prosit Idea
  Service -> Groq: prompt + transcript
  Groq --> Service: prosit suggestion
also Appel 5 — Flashcards SM-2
  Service -> Groq: prompt + transcript
  Groq --> Service: cards 8-12
end

== Persistance résultats ==

Service -> DB: AutoPrepJob.update(jobId, {\n  status: 'completed',\n  results: { ... }\n})
activate DB
DB --> Service: ok
deactivate DB
deactivate Service

== Polling front + affichage ==

Front -> API: GET /api/auto-prep-jobs/:jobId\n(toutes les 3s)
API -> DB: AutoPrepJob.findById
activate DB
DB --> API: job complet
deactivate DB
API --> Front: { status: 'completed', results }
deactivate API
Front --> Prof: 5 sections avec toggles\n[Garder] / [Rejeter]

== Validation par le prof ==

Prof -> Front: décoche éléments non pertinents,\nclique "Publier"
activate Front
Front -> API: POST /api/auto-prep-jobs/:jobId/publish\n{ selections }
activate API

== Création atomique entités ==

API -> DB: insert QCM
API -> DB: insert VideoQuestion[]
API -> DB: update Course.learningOutcomes
API -> DB: insert Prosit (statut: 'brouillon')
API -> DB: insert Deck + Cards SM-2

API --> Front: 200 ok
deactivate API
Front --> Prof: "Publié — 1 QCM, 3 questions in-video,\n5 outcomes, 1 cas pratique brouillon, 10 flashcards"
deactivate Front

note over Service #FFFAE6
  Coût : ~30-60 secondes pour le prof
  vs ~2-3 heures de travail manuel.
  Quota free tier Groq : largement
  suffisant pour usage pédagogique.
end note

@enduml
